    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Patching and Dependency Hygiene with Trivy and Gradle',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains patching and dependency hygiene with Trivy and Gradle, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] A lock file records the exact version of every library a program uses. [[slnc 300]] A bill of materials lists them in a form that scanners understand. [[slnc 300]] And a scanner compares that list with known problems. [[slnc 600]] Think of a shop that keeps a list of every ingredient, with brand and batch number. [[slnc 300]] An inspector arrives with this morning's recall notices, and marks every product that contains a recalled batch. [[slnc 300]] And a delivery's label is checked against the list before anything is used. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online store. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will hear how a scanner's report is read. [[slnc 300]] What to fix first, and to which version. [[slnc 300]] And what a scanner cannot tell you."),
